{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791054329,"nonce":"sAWCI7cRZdK/hoCwX7UTVMKOofQ=","title":"Haxe 5 std, step 1: haxe.runtime.Copy, haxe.UInt32, haxe.ds.Int64Map, ValueType.TInt64","message":"First step of Haxe 5 support (decision recorded on 3f6e9e7). Vendored unchanged from the corpus pin's std/ (7f87f746; std is MIT): haxe/runtime/Copy.hx, haxe/UInt32.hx, haxe/ds/Int64Map.hx. Type.hx's ValueType gains TInt64 in its Haxe 5 position, and the runtime TVALUETYPE ordinals are renumbered to match (the compiler builds ValueType from Type.hx, so only the runtime held ordinals). There is no Int64 box tag, so `Type.typeof` on a statically Int64 argument answers TInt64 from the static type (`haxe_type_typeof_int64`); Issue12264, which passed only because `TInt64` used to be a capture pattern, keeps passing.\n\nFixed on the way:\n- `var o:O = cast {}` with O a type parameter vanished: an empty `{}` is an empty block to the parser, and only a Dynamic/structural expected type made it an object. A cast's operand is a value, so `cast {}` is now always an empty object.\n- bind-time locals are immutable symbols (captured by value).\n\nGate: 823 -\u003e 824 (Issue11863), 0 lost; Issue12538 COMPILE_FAIL -\u003e WRONG_ANSWER; suite 207/0/1; fixtures, integration tests, clippy, runtime tests clean.\n\nCopy's generic methods still trap when not inlined (455f956: body-only type parameters, generics called from generics). Issue2990 needs typeString of UInt32 operators; TestBasetypes needs more.","files":null}]}